  "nl_text": "The rschema_0432 database is designed to manage information about students, professors, courses, and departments within an educational institution. The database consists of five tables: student, professor, course, course_registration, and department. The student table stores information about each student, including their unique student ID, name, address, enrollment year, date of birth, and the department they belong to, which is linked to the department table through a foreign key that allows for cascading updates and deletions. The professor table contains details about each professor, such as their unique professor ID, name, office number, office start time, and the department they belong to, also linked to the department table. The course table holds information about each course, including its unique course ID, name, semester, year, teaching professor ID, class day, course duration, and the department it belongs to, with foreign keys linking it to both the professor and department tables. The course_registration table tracks the registration of students for specific courses, with a composite primary key consisting of the student ID, registration time, and course ID, and foreign keys linking it to both the student and course tables. The department table stores basic information about each department, including its unique department ID and name.",
  "gold_question": "The teaching management system of a university is as follows: The university comprises multiple departments, with department information including Department ID and Department Name. Each department has several students, with student information including Student ID, Name, Address, Enrollment Year, and Date of Birth. The university also has several professors, with professor information including Professor ID, Name, Office Number, and Office Start Time. The university offers multiple courses, with course information including Course ID, Course Name, Semester, Year, Teaching Professor, Class Day, and Course Duration. Students can register for courses, with registration information including Registration Time, Course ID, and Student ID.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0432.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0432\nCREATE TABLE `student` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `enrollment_year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `student_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `professor` (\n  `professor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `office_number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `office_start_time` time DEFAULT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`professor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `professor_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course` (\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `semester` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  `teaching_professor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `class_day` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `course_duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`course_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`teaching_professor_id`) REFERENCES `professor` (`professor_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `course_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `course_registration` (\n  `student_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `course_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`student_id`, `registration_time`, `course_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `course_registration_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`student_id`) REFERENCES `student` (`student_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `course_registration_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`course_id`) REFERENCES `course` (`course_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
